## Result: identical in all 3 runs. 200 acceleration steps per run: 150 at stamp = 1 ms mod 10 ms and 50 at 2 ms mod 10 ms (the braking
## steps are split over two physics steps, consistent with the fixture, TS-027_C4_validation.log Stage 1b). The output stamped t contains the
## physical velocity change of 8-9 ms earlier: delay histogram {8 ms: 50, 9 ms: 150}. The original 100 Hz IMU sampled stamps = 0 mod 10 ms,
## i.e. never a step (TS-027). The FIR group delay of a 10-sample mean (4.5 ms) applies to acceleration spread evenly over the block;
## with the 100 Hz command hold the physical step sits at the block start.
